Study design: Published cohort studies, case-control studies, and cross-sectional studies, only English and Chinese.
Study subjects: Patients with OMDs diagnosed by clinical examination combined with histopathology, with explicit diagnostic criteria:
RAU: conforming to the clinical features of “yellow, red, depressed, painful” as described in Oral Mucosal Diseases, excluding traumatic ulcers, Beçhet’s disease, and other similar disorders;
OLP: meeting the World Health Organization (WHO) diagnostic criteria, with typical reticular/erosive lesions and histopathological manifestations of “sawtooth-shaped epithelium and band-like lymphocyte infiltration”;
OLK: consistent with premalignant lesion diagnostic criteria, excluding reversible white lesions caused by local irritants;
OSF: diagnosed based on clinical symptoms (mouth opening restriction, mucosal pallor and fibrosis) and histopathology.

